.\" Manpage for auto-updates.conf.
.\" Process with: groff -man -Tascii auto-updates.conf.5
.TH AUTO-UPDATES.CONF 5 "29 September 2026" "auto-updates 1.2.3" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
auto-updates.conf \- Configuration file for the auto-updates automated package service
.SH SYNOPSIS
/etc/auto-updates/auto-updates.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B auto-updates.conf
is the main configuration file for the \fBauto-updates\fR automated package manager service.
It defines update modes, execution schedules, reboot policies, notification emitters, and
logging options.
.PP
The file uses a standard shell-compatible key-value syntax:
.RS
.B KEY=\fIvalue\fR
.RE
Lines beginning with \fB#\fR are treated as comments and ignored.
.SH CONFIGURATION DIRECTIVES
.TP
.BR MODE = \fI{security|all|weekly-all|daily-all}\fR
Specifies the automated update policy.
.RS
.TP
.B security
Downloads and applies only security-related updates every day. Default setting.
.TP
.B all
Applies full system upgrades across all packages every day at the scheduled time.
.TP
.B weekly-all \fR(or \fBall-weekly\fR)
Runs daily security updates Monday through Saturday, and a full system upgrade of all
packages once per week on \fBWEEKLY_DAY\fR.
.TP
.B daily-all
Backward-compatible alias for \fBall\fR.
.RE
.TP
.BR SCHEDULE_TIME = \fIHH:MM\fR
Defines the local time of day in 24-hour format when updates are initiated. Default is \fB03:30\fR.
.TP
.BR WEEKLY_DAY = \fI{Sun|Mon|Tue|Wed|Thu|Fri|Sat}\fR
Specifies the day of the week on which full system upgrades are executed when \fBMODE\fR
is set to \fBweekly-all\fR. Default is \fBSun\fR.
.TP
.BR REBOOT = \fI{never|when-needed|when-changed}\fR
Configures automated system reboot behavior following package installations.
.RS
.TP
.B never
Do not reboot automatically. Default setting.
.TP
.B when-needed
Reboot only when installed packages require a restart (such as kernel or glibc updates).
.TP
.B when-changed
Reboot whenever any package has been installed or upgraded (recommended for appliance or kiosk hosts).
.RE
.TP
.BR REBOOT_DELAY = \fIMINUTES\fR
Delay in minutes before initiating a reboot when \fBREBOOT\fR is enabled. Setting this
to \fB0\fR triggers an immediate reboot via \fBsystemctl reboot\fR (recommended for virtual
machines and servers). Setting this to an integer \fBN\fR schedules a delayed reboot
(\fBshutdown -r +N\fR) with a wall broadcast warning. Default is \fB0\fR.
.TP
.BR DEFER_REBOOT_IF_BUSY = \fI{true|false}\fR
When set to \fBtrue\fR (default), checks whether compilation tasks (e.g., \fBrpmbuild\fR,
\fBmake\fR, \fBcargo\fR, \fBninja\fR, \fBgcc\fR, container builds) or \fBsystemd-inhibit\fR locks
are running. If detected, reboot is safely postponed until the next cycle.
.TP
.BR REFRESH_METADATA = \fI{true|false}\fR
When set to \fBtrue\fR (default), forces DNF to query upstream repository mirrors for fresh
metadata before every update run, bypassing cached metadata expiration windows.
.TP
.BR INCLUDE_PHASED_UPDATES = \fI{true|false}\fR
When set to \fBtrue\fR, passes \fB-o APT::Get::Always-Include-Phased-Updates=true\fR on Ubuntu
and Debian systems to apply phased packages immediately. When set to \fBfalse\fR (default),
Ubuntu gradual phased rollout policies are respected.
.TP
.BR RANDOM_SLEEP = \fISECONDS\fR
Maximum randomized delay in seconds introduced before executing DNF commands. Prevents
simultaneous mirror load spikes across large fleets. Default is \fB10\fR.
.TP
.BR EMIT_VIA = \fI{stdio|motd|email}\fR
Controls how update notices and completion reports are delivered. Default is \fBstdio\fR.
.TP
.BR EMAIL_TO = \fIrecipient@domain.com\fR
Destination email address when \fBEMIT_VIA=email\fR.
.TP
.BR EMAIL_FROM = \fIsender@domain.com\fR
Originating email address when \fBEMIT_VIA=email\fR.
.TP
.BR EMAIL_HOST = \fIsmtp.domain.com\fR
SMTP relay hostname when \fBEMIT_VIA=email\fR.
.TP
.BR LOG_FILE = \fIPATH\fR
Specifies the destination path for execution logs. Default is \fB/var/log/auto-updates.log\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
A workstation configuration performing daily security updates with weekly full Sunday updates
and automated reboots when needed:
.PP
.RS
.nf
MODE=weekly-all
SCHEDULE_TIME=03:30
WEEKLY_DAY=Sun
REBOOT=when-needed
REBOOT_DELAY=0
DEFER_REBOOT_IF_BUSY=true
REFRESH_METADATA=true
RANDOM_SLEEP=10
EMIT_VIA=stdio
LOG_FILE=/var/log/auto-updates.log
.fi
.RE
.SH VIRTUAL MACHINE AND HYPERVISOR ARCHITECTURES
When running \fBauto-updates\fR inside a virtual machine, the host hypervisor configuration
determines whether unattended overnight reboots succeed or stall. Linux virtualization relies
on two main execution models:
.PP
.nf
+-------------------------+-------------------------------+-------------------------------+
| Feature                 | GNOME Boxes (qemu:///session) | System Libvirt (qemu:///system)|
+-------------------------+-------------------------------+-------------------------------+
| Intended Use            | Desktop user app / ISO testing| Servers, CI/CD, 24/7 nodes    |
| Execution Context       | User session (UID 1000)       | System daemon (virtqemud/root)|
| Tied to Desktop?        | Yes (GNOME Shell, screen lock)| No (headless system daemon)   |
| Survives Screen Lock?   | Often no (power-saving pauses)| Yes (independent of desktop)  |
| Host Autostart Support? | No (requires graphical login) | Native (virsh autostart)      |
| Guest Reboot Handling   | Tied to display window/SPICE  | Handled by hypervisor daemon  |
+-------------------------+-------------------------------+-------------------------------+
.fi
.SS GNOME Boxes Best Practices
For desktop development VMs running under GNOME Boxes (\fBqemu:///session\fR):
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRun in Background\fR: Ensure \fB"Run in background"\fR is enabled in GNOME Boxes preferences
so that closing the window or locking the screen does not suspend the virtual machine.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBReboot Delay\fR: Keep \fBREBOOT_DELAY=0\fR so that reboot is executed immediately via
\fBsystemctl reboot\fR rather than delaying 5 minutes.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHost Power Management\fR: Ensure the hypervisor host system does not enter sleep or suspend
during the scheduled update window (\fBSCHEDULE_TIME\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBLifecycle Policy\fR: Verify that the guest domain XML specifies
\fB<on_reboot>restart</on_reboot>\fR (not \fBdestroy\fR).
.SS Enterprise and Production Recommendations
For 24/7 production hosts, build orchestration nodes, and CI/CD runners, migrate to
\fBSystem Libvirt\fR (\fBqemu:///system\fR) managed by \fBvirt-manager\fR, Cockpit, or \fBvirsh\fR:
.PP
.RS
.nf
virsh --connect qemu:///system autostart <domain-name>
.fi
.RE
.PP
System Libvirt VMs run independently of graphical desktop sessions, survive desktop sleep and
screen locks, start automatically at physical host power-on, and re-post virtual BIOS/GRUB
immediately upon reboot.
